## Control {{controlId}}: Develop, Document, and Periodically Update System Security Plans

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization develops, documents, and maintains the System Security Plan within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through automated SSP generation, continuous monitoring, and periodic review documented in "SSP Maintenance Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

**SSP Content:**
The System Security Plan describes:
- **System Boundary:** M365 GCC High tenant ({{primaryDomain}}) including Exchange Online, SharePoint Online, Teams, Intune, Defender, and Entra ID
- **Environment of Operation:** Microsoft Azure Government (GCC High) with FedRAMP High baseline inheritance
- **Security Requirements:** Implementation status of all 110 CMMC Level 2 practices
- **Interconnections:** Documented connections with external systems per CA.L2-3.12.2 and CA.L2-3.12.3

{{#if secureScoresAvailable}}
**SSP Metrics:**
Current security posture: Secure Score **{{currentScore}}** / {{maxScore}} ({{percentage}}%) — referenced in SSP executive summary.
{{/if}}

**SSP Maintenance:**
- **Update Triggers:** System changes, assessment findings, new CMMC guidance, organizational changes
- **Annual Review:** Comprehensive SSP review and update at least annually
- **Automated Generation:** Evidence Ops toolchain generates SSP control narratives from live assessment data
- **Version Control:** SSP versions tracked with change history and approval signatures

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Annual SSP review and update; triggered updates upon significant changes; automated narrative generation
- **Frequency:** Annual review, triggered updates as needed
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** SSP Maintenance Policy v1.0, SSP Change Log

**Review Frequency:** Annually by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine current SSP document, revision history, change log, automated generation configuration, and annual review records.

